# Copy to `.env.cloudflare` (gitignored). Read by `scripts/cf`, the wrapper
# every wrangler command in this repo goes through — so these apply to this
# project only, not to your other Cloudflare work.

# The account this repo deploys to. Pin it: without it, a deploy lands in
# whichever account happens to be signed in, and with several accounts that is
# a coin flip. `pnpm cf whoami` prints the id after you sign in.
# This must be the account that owns the alzheimers.dev zone.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# Optional, and required for anything DNS: wrangler's browser login cannot
# grant DNS write (`dns_records:write` isn't in its OAuth scope list), so
# attaching a custom domain over existing records needs a token.
#
# Create a token at https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens (or the
# account's API Tokens page) → Create Token → Custom token, with:
#   Account → Workers Scripts → Edit
#   Zone    → Workers Routes  → Edit
#   Zone    → DNS             → Edit   <- required for custom domains
#   Zone Resources: Include → Specific zone → alzheimers.dev
#
# User tokens and account-owned tokens both work; they differ only in which
# endpoint verifies them (/user/tokens/verify vs
# /accounts/<id>/tokens/verify), which matters when debugging a 'not valid'
# response — an account-owned token looks invalid to the user endpoint. Token
# values carry a prefix (e.g. `cfat…`). Tokens are editable after creation, so
# a missing permission is a dashboard edit, not a new token.
#
# Careful: a token set here OUTRANKS the `pnpm cf login` session. A wrong or
# expired value breaks every `pnpm cf` command, including deploys that would
# otherwise work — comment this line out to fall back to the browser session.
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
